#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345288 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ffe2816-aae7-59ca-9562-412dd652a6c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342376} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb81157-2ab8-5ec8-a9fa-335547e6606a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342605} {:answer/id #uuid "519f8d58-aa96-5048-9d82-8885955e1cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342913} {:answer/id #uuid "5ee0276d-41f4-5591-b923-85e85120cdc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343039} {:answer/id #uuid "988c1583-846c-502f-b92b-7cb927f59f72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ffe2816-aae7-59ca-9562-412dd652a6c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342376} :answer-field/id #uuid "890c712d-24f5-52cb-9fc0-29be52e23fa4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "707c9a96-8c3c-57b1-ae5a-3037250afe04" :question/math-academy-id "q-77220" :question/problem "![](images/2e/2efa774a3a7e97c23f695cfbdf681b53df055b8a84b84e2729af0a565841aeb7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=1$ to $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,,4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}+{(4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t>0$ for $t\\in [1,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2(4-1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45ba9575-4116-5da1-9d13-75fddafe1880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342813} {:answer/id #uuid "56459a3a-433a-5d89-a00c-d2db7f4af24d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342956} {:answer/id #uuid "b56ab6d7-6374-51b8-a73a-573a9c6d25f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343828} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d83a2c-baf4-5473-8f83-d89b478ba56a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344213} {:answer/id #uuid "ebf2aebc-fe9e-54f8-8ae7-fef78f976954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56459a3a-433a-5d89-a00c-d2db7f4af24d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342956} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a05ee8c-a6f2-5705-ac77-f7c2d74908f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c996c916-6d56-55b9-8504-9c0842874c89" :question/math-academy-id "q-77427" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,x,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,-x,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=10.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & x & 1 \\\\ 1 & -x & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}x & 1 \\\\ -x & 3\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}2 & x \\\\ 1 & -x\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(3x+x)i-(6-1)j+(-2x-x)k \\\\  & =⟨4x,-5,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+25+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =10 \\\\ \\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)} & =10 \\\\ 25({x}^{2}+1) & =100 \\\\ {x}^{2}+1 & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345296 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00fa6337-ab0d-5160-a611-2ddc8da0cf63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342253} {:answer/id #uuid "09269469-cfd9-5d57-8d8b-42fdb071211c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342313} {:answer/id #uuid "23a6c0cd-5de2-535e-b93e-c6aa000f9907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342534} {:answer/id #uuid "51e0ea9c-50b6-5b70-92d8-61c5f756d8a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342915} {:answer/id #uuid "f6c26781-a599-5f95-bd31-c91372b3df28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23a6c0cd-5de2-535e-b93e-c6aa000f9907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342534} :answer-field/id #uuid "0083fa75-a1b0-5b25-a910-a26f765c9e50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d7c9e319-7861-5d4f-b23a-d86c9fbc5eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-77429" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,0,-4⟩,$ $b=⟨-1,1,2x⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=2\\sqrt{5}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2x\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 2x\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(0+4)i-(4x-4)j+(2-0)k \\\\  & =⟨4,-4x+4,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4x+4)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16{x}^{2}-32x+16+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-32x+36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-32x+36} & =2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-32x+36 & =20 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-32x+16 & =0 \\\\ 16({x}^{2}-2x+1) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+1 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x-1 & =0 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348163 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56c69cb0-7f0e-5e35-986d-158b61077274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346089} {:answer/id #uuid "71c5b9f9-6633-53db-81a3-5e202fd94284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346358} {:answer/id #uuid "7b1c54d3-c72c-51f0-9b10-d971c775781f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346427} {:answer/id #uuid "d30ab4a2-a099-5d28-9260-d3ae4a007ac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347197} {:answer/id #uuid "f880d89a-4990-525d-b959-a376bd6c02a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56c69cb0-7f0e-5e35-986d-158b61077274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346089} :answer-field/id #uuid "b53311d9-adbd-5c51-9d52-3ec08a70b72c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347923}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8fed8466-eb7a-5364-abdc-283bfaec0630" :question/math-academy-id "q-79161" :question/problem "Which of the following parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate a circle of radius $2$ centered at the point $(1,6)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $2$ centered at the point $(1,6).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fdaa562-e749-5638-b8bf-7d6aecb9b18b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -6,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345898} {:answer/id #uuid "651f35c1-e6b4-5d04-ad03-e2acabd396f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +6,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346232} {:answer/id #uuid "9efcc203-2d31-5282-9de7-f79dab0bc92a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346739} {:answer/id #uuid "ad1724ab-1f59-527d-b4e4-0bb0231978d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +6,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346861} {:answer/id #uuid "d4732e46-c796-5948-8076-46b9343587a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4732e46-c796-5948-8076-46b9343587a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347212} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1ff9986-e20a-5596-a660-510964475da7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9fcfe226-c7b7-59ed-a771-6da8d179c26a" :question/math-academy-id "q-79164" :question/problem "Which of the following parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate a circle of radius $1$ centered at the point $(4,-6)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $1$ centered at the point $(4,-6).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -6,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10bc0c2e-b811-53c7-9a39-a3a742a76a4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{4}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345494} {:answer/id #uuid "16bdfa20-b41b-5459-b61c-04f948ff3534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345552} {:answer/id #uuid "58da2168-0c36-5490-ba1e-943612f0bccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{5\\pi }{4}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346116} {:answer/id #uuid "918f45dd-e507-51a9-9661-5c366ab69a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346623} {:answer/id #uuid "d06d8135-2704-5d9a-a92a-9f45781af4eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "918f45dd-e507-51a9-9661-5c366ab69a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346623} :answer-field/id #uuid "102a7531-0b8e-53d3-81b9-e0c840da2063" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347637}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f6f6736e-3f23-5f6c-b5db-0f4b217b048e" :question/math-academy-id "q-79165" :question/problem "![](images/c9/c9e8fb87758eefb1facfea08112c5add0cc54d481e36e740d3cc623f05fa41fb.png)\n\nThe arc of a circle above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$  centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=2.$ So, the parametric equations of the *full* circle are \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to the arc above, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the circle and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/8a/8a0491010e71d24ebac54b5b8d03b1ce45f7de90a0f21ff1ea2f0c2babf4ec77.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}]$, we get the required arc of the circle.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the arc of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f4aac57-3f1b-57f2-a3ff-9d8faaa0e509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345626} {:answer/id #uuid "7278bdb7-676e-5957-8898-bc674a8aab37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346365} {:answer/id #uuid "92e81177-f50d-5b64-80d1-6cc55345482e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346638} {:answer/id #uuid "bb66022b-c77a-5186-a4d6-369a992b45c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346975} {:answer/id #uuid "c4e3f4c0-87e3-567c-9abd-804a86cf121d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{3\\pi }{4}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f4aac57-3f1b-57f2-a3ff-9d8faaa0e509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345626} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cdb5a75-c952-53df-87e2-34262d973593" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860