rameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the circle and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/97/9752e135eee9c4e585a007f84b0b8b8d220d4e2e1f027fc8a69aebf27066940e.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\frac{5\\pi }{4}]$, we get the required arc of the circle.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the arc of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{5\\pi }{4}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41f4c8c5-a1e0-50d2-90e3-c842b69b61a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345916} {:answer/id #uuid "8be8bc87-925d-5a80-b272-9812c2eb7b96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346563} {:answer/id #uuid "b024a727-8b31-5d76-a59f-dbb3e082e615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346889} {:answer/id #uuid "fac11c48-254b-548d-81fb-bf48b11a35c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347566} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7ffdeb-b39d-53fd-a335-3c0a492a7c63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41f4c8c5-a1e0-50d2-90e3-c842b69b61a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345916} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f4d4e4d-7b06-5451-ae6d-dff63e644b63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e2b98504-334c-5f63-b626-52b1babf6c47" :question/math-academy-id "q-79170" :question/problem "![](images/14/1407fa82fd00d07311cb34c6a3d5f0d0c79808d321d049d74114a6f4f2e5f6a6.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $2$ centered at $(3,2)$, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(5,2)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r+a,b).$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $2$ centered at the point $(3,2).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22305542-a066-54f5-9dc3-0148cf233e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345658} {:answer/id #uuid "8842098a-961f-5d95-855d-da37bf92fb2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=2\\opera